            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SmartSoup1503"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I substituted 1/2 Stevia for sugar and it was great. Key to success is the instant Tapioca - absorbs all the juices. Also another tip is to put an egg wash on the top a bottom of the pie crust and bake it on a pie sheet that is heated with the oven. Assures the bottom crust is baked.",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-21T13:07:37.494Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "trillian01"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this as a treat for my father on Thanksgiving yesterday. While he was more interested in a different pie, two others tried this kind for the first time and declared it a new favorite. Since it was getting baked the same time as another pie, this went in for 15 min at 425°, then about an hour longer at 350°. Not at all runny nor geletin like. I cut the rhubarb to about 1 cm pieces and they cooked perfectly inside the pie. I may have used slightly less tapioca, but only because I didn't measure. It was in the fridge for about 4 hours before serving which made it set perfectly.",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-27T19:06:28.887Z"
          },
          {
